    <string name="root_dialog_title">Root access required</string>
    <string name="root_dialog_body">Upload turns this device into the transfer source. The console connects back on TCP 1004 and TCP 1005, and discovery listens on UDP 1006 — ports below 1024, which Android reserves. On most devices this needs root (Magisk/KernelSU): GarlicTransfer will run sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start=1004 as root so only the transfer ports are opened, and restore it afterwards. Without root, the transfer can only proceed if your kernel already allows low ports.</string>
